    The same sha256 on a second build.
    Its lowers of wasi:sockets/types@0.3.0 (wasm-tools print): [method]udp-socket.send and [method]udp-socket.receive
    with the async option, memory and realloc; [static]udp-socket.create, bind, connect, the two address getters,
    the hop limit's and the buffer sizes' getters and setters with no async option, with memory and realloc. It
    lowers no disconnect and no get-address-family: std reaches neither. It cancels a subtask with the sync
    subtask.cancel. Its `run` is async-typed and lifted with no async option.
    wasmtime's trace of it (WASMTIME_LOG=wasmtime_wasi=trace) shows wasi-libc keeping a receive pending across the
    read timeout and the nonblocking recv, and the next recv taking that receive's result: neither is cancelled.

